# trivy misconfiguration ignores — intentional, documented architectural decisions.
# Each maps to a decision in docs/architecture.md "Security model — honest framing".
# Revisit on every provider bump. Everything NOT listed here hard-fails CI.

# AWS-0053 — "Load balancer is exposed publicly" (aws_lb.internal = false).
# DELIBERATE v1 decision: internet-facing ALB whose ingress SG admits ONLY the VUIT
# VPN managed prefix list (no 0.0.0.0/0 ingress). The stronger internal-ALB topology
# is the documented future option, gated on VUIT routing the VPN into the VPC.
AVD-AWS-0053

# AWS-0104 — "unrestricted egress" (app SG: 443 to 0.0.0.0/0).
# DELIBERATE: the instance must reach ECR/registry (image pulls), Secrets Manager,
# SSM, and IdP metadata over the NAT; those endpoints have no stable, pinnable CIDR.
# Tightening this to VPC interface endpoints is the documented hardening follow-up.
AVD-AWS-0104

# AWS-0136 — "Topic encryption does not use a customer managed key".
# The alarms topic is encrypted with the AWS-managed SNS key (alias/aws/sns). A
# customer-managed CMK (key policy + rotation + cost) is unwarranted for ops
# alarm metadata; AWS-managed encryption is the deliberate choice.
AVD-AWS-0136
